  "body": "## What happens\n\n1. Open the Stock page of a setup. Select **From model** and a source model.\n2. The page shows **Fit margin** and **Fit to Models**. Both are enabled.\n3. Click **Fit to Models**. The app refuses with this message:\n   `from-model stock follows its source: choose Box or Cylinder to fit`\n4. Select **Box**. The red message stays on the page until the next action. It now refers to a mode that is not selected.\n\nThe refusal is correct (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`, `CommandKind::StockFit` with `shape == 2`). The stock does not change. But the page shows a control that cannot work in this mode. A user clicks it and gets an error.\n\n## Expected\n\n- In **From model** mode, the page does not show **Fit margin** and **Fit to Models**, or it shows them disabled with a hover text that says why.\n- A change of the stock shape clears the old fit refusal.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Build: v0.19.0 (cfd96ab1), Windows, release build, 2026-11-14.\n- Model: `testdata/models/Milling-test.step`. The from-model refusal is correct. **Box** + **Fit to Models** gives 63.998 x 53.719 x 29 mm, Z bottom -7 mm (2 mm margin on each side). That is correct.\n- The structural test `crates/ui/tests/shell.rs` (`follows its source`) pins the refusal. No test pins the visible or enabled state of the button in this mode.\n\n## Suggested triage\n\nLabels suggested by the AGENTS.md tables: `P7` (owed polish, no wrong output), `effort:low` (one UI page, no new logic), `area:ui`, `source:agent` (an agent filed it for the reporter). I cannot set labels on this repository.\n\nDone means: in **From model** mode, the page does not offer **Fit to Models** as an action that can work. A structural test in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs` asserts that state. A change of the stock shape clears the fit refusal.\n",
